+# HANDOFF: inventory ledger (gap "inventory is not authoritative and never decrements")
+
+Worktree: `/home/user/yallternative-living/.claude/worktrees/agent-ac7c54fc0d2ada1a2`
+Branch: `worktree-agent-ac7c54fc0d2ada1a2` (branched from `main`, merged `claude/website-world-class-gaps-ox05mw` twice: at start and again at head `f76a116`). Nothing pushed.
+
+## Done and verified (before the second merge -- see "Half-done" for what the merge changed)
+
+Verified green at commit `WIP: inventory tests, suite counts` + formatting: `npm run format`, `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm test` (unit pool + qa-check 1128), `npm run test:smoke` (26/26), `node scripts/extended_qa_test.js` (PASSED), `node scripts/a11y-check.js` (0 violations, 37 pages x 2 themes).
+
+- `workers/schema.sql` + `workers/state/migrations.js`: schema v7 -- tables `inventory(product_id PK, on_hand, reserved, seed_stock, updated_at)` with `CHECK (reserved >= 0 AND reserved <= on_hand)` (the oversell guard) and `inventory_holds(session_id, product_id, qty, state, created_at, updated_at; PK(session_id, product_id))`, index `inventory_holds_state`. schema.sql/migrations parity test passes.
+- `workers/state/inventory.js` (D1): `trackedProductsOf`, `syncInventory` (lazy seed; owner correction = products.json stock != seed_stock -> on_hand = MAX(new stock, reserved), seed_stock = new stock; per-isolate memo on catalog signature, `resetInventoryMemo()` test seam), `readAvailability`/`availableCounts`, `reserveInventory` (one `db.batch`, all-or-nothing, CHECK refuses the race loser, throws `InventoryError` `insufficient_stock` naming the product / `hold_exists`), `commitInventory` (active->committed: on_hand -= qty, reserved -= qty; returns `soldOut` ids), `releaseInventory` (active->released: reserved -= qty), `restockInventory` (committed->restocked: on_hand += qty), `sweepStaleHolds` (25h backstop), `inventorySnapshot`, `inventoryRows`/`holdRows`. Every transition is keyed on the current state, so redeliveries are no-ops.
+- `workers/routes/inventory.js`: `handleInventory` (GET /api/inventory -> `{products:{id:{available,tracked:true}}}` tracked-only, no-store, rate limit 30/min/IP fail-open, 503 without STATE_DB or catalog), `availabilityForCheckout` (null on any error -> static stock), `holdsFromAllocation`, `reserveForCheckout` (fail OPEN on DB error, `{ok:false, refusal}` on a lost race in the `unavailableDetails` shape: `{id, reason:"sold_out"}` or `{id:"custom-box", reason:"member_unavailable", member}`), `unwindRefusedSession` (delete coupon, expire session x2, error log), `announceSoldOut` (console.error `[INVENTORY_SOLD_OUT]` + TODO for alertOwner), `commitInventoryForSession`, `releaseInventoryForSession`, `restockInventoryForRefund` (full refund only; looks the session up by payment_intent). All log lines carry `[INVENTORY]`.
+- `workers/checkout.js` (thin hooks): import block; `allocateStock(items, catalog, availability)` now takes the ledger's `Map<id, available>` and returns `holds` per line; `handleCheckout` calls `availabilityForCheckout` before `allocateStock`, then right after the Stripe session exists (BEFORE the gift-card hold) `reserveForCheckout` -> on refusal `unwindRefusedSession` + `ClientError(400, unavailableDetails)` (cart.js drops the line on 400 + `unavailable`); ROUTES gains `"/inventory"`; the fetch dispatcher allows GET for `/inventory`; `scheduled()` gains an "inventory hold sweep" step.
+- `workers/routes/stripe-webhook.js` (thin hooks, each in its own try/catch pushed to `failures`): completed -> `commitInventoryForSession`; expired and async_payment_failed -> `releaseInventoryForSession`; charge.refunded -> `restockInventoryForRefund`.
+- `assets/js/main.js`: `lowStockBadgeHTML`, `applyLiveInventory` (overrides `stock` in place for tracked products only), `fetchLiveInventory` (one GET per page load, honours CMS `site.showLiveStock === false`, skips file://), `refreshLiveCards` (re-renders only changed `article.card[data-id]`, keeps `.in`), `applyLiveStockToPdp` (Sold Out swap / max-qty cap / `.pdp-live-stock` badge). Shop hook where the old Snipcart-overlay comment was; PDP hook after `initPdpPage()`. Exports `applyLiveInventory`, `lowStockBadgeHTML`, `LIVE_INVENTORY_URL`.
+- `assets/css/styles.css`: `.pdp-live-stock { margin-bottom: 0.75rem }`.
+- CMS: `admin/config.yml` product `stock` hint rewritten (explains counting down + editing resets the live count); new Site settings field `showLiveStock` ("Shop · Show live stock counts", default true) with hint. `assets/data/content.json` `site.showLiveStock: true` (build-data regenerated `content-data.js`). `docs/EDITING-GUIDE.md`: "The count runs itself" paragraph + table rows.
+- Tests: `scripts/worker-inventory.test.js` (96 assertions: seed, correction re-seed, reserve, race via CHECK, commit/release/restock exactly-once, sweep, checkout cap/refusal/box/fail-open/no-DB, webhook hooks incl. partial vs full refund, /api/inventory shape + no-store + rate limit + 503). `scripts/worker-checkout.test.js` +7 (ledger-bound seam). `scripts/main.test.js` +12 (`applyLiveInventory`). README/AGENTS counts bumped.
+
+## Half-done (state at HEAD `e7faa78`)
+
+The second merge of `claude/website-world-class-gaps-ox05mw` (brings `workers/routes/alerts.js` with `alertOwner(env, ctx, alert)`, `scripts/worker-alerts.test.js`, JS/CSS minification) was committed with two hand-resolved conflicts and has NOT been re-verified:
+- `sw.js`: took the branch's `CACHE_NAME`; it is content-hashed, so `npm run build-data` must regenerate it.
+- `AGENTS.md` step-4 row: set to 49 suites / 1128 qa-check assertions by hand. `README.md` still says 48 / "(50 with verification gates)" from before the merge -- recount: `ls scripts/*.test.js | grep -v browser | wc -l`.
+- `workers/routes/inventory.js` `announceSoldOut`: still the TODO; wire `alertOwner(env, ctx, { key: "inventory-sold-out:<productId>", subject, details })` now that alerts.js exists. `commitInventoryForSession(session, env)` has no `ctx` -- add a `ctx` parameter and pass it from the webhook's completed branch (`processStripeEvent(event, env, ctx)` has it).
+
+## Next steps, in order
+
+1. `npm run build-data` (fixes `sw.js` CACHE_NAME, regenerates derived files).
+2. Wire `alertOwner` in `announceSoldOut` (above); remove the TODO; add one assertion in `scripts/worker-inventory.test.js` section 6 that a sold-out commit calls it (worker-alerts.test.js shows how alerts are captured).
+3. Fix README.md counts (49 suites), confirm AGENTS.md row; qa-check count is whatever `npm test` prints.
+4. `npm run format && npm run lint && npm run format:check && npm test && npm run test:smoke && node scripts/extended_qa_test.js && node scripts/a11y-check.js`.
+5. Squash the WIP commits into one clean commit (no model names). Do not push unless told.
+
+## Known traps
+
+- `workers/checkout.js` and `workers/routes/stripe-webhook.js` are edited by other branches (catch blocks / alerts); keep the inventory hooks as the thin calls they are and re-merge before finishing.
+- `syncInventory` memo is module-level: tests MUST call `resetInventoryMemo()` per fresh DB (`freshDb()` in the suite does).
+- `reserveInventory` skips products with no inventory row -- seed (`syncInventory`) must run first; `availabilityForCheckout` does that on the live path.
+- The gift-card hold failure path (409) leaves the inventory hold `active` until Stripe's `checkout.session.expired` for the expired session or the 25h sweep -- deliberate, not a bug.
+- The unit pool's `worker-state.test.js` enforces schema.sql <-> migrations.js parity; keep both in sync.
+- D1 `batch` is the transaction; the emulator's `batch` uses BEGIN/ROLLBACK, so constraint atomicity is really tested.
+
+## Dashboard steps
+
+None beyond the existing `STATE_DB` D1 binding in `workers/wrangler.toml` (the migration applies itself on first request). No new env vars, secrets, or bindings.
